IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch6-liability.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 6 "Auditors' liability": ss 532, 533, 534, 535, 536, 537, 538, 538A
-- (lines 7464-7538 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively. See coa12-ch3a-report.l4 for how to read an answer.
-- Forks are in NOTES.md. Keel and other-part answers are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.
-- The regulations the Secretary of State may make under ss 535 and 538 are outside the sources: what they require is an INPUT.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 532  Voidness of provisions protecting auditors from liability
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 532(1), s 532(1)(a), s 532(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the section applies to a provision that exempts an auditor from liability for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in the course of the audit, and to one by which the company (directly or indirectly) indemnifies its auditor, or the auditor of an associated company, against such liability.
-- src:7467 | (1) This section applies to any provision—
-- src:7468 | (a) for exempting an auditor of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company occurring in the course of the audit of accounts, or
-- src:7469 | (b) by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against any liability attaching to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is auditor occurring in the course of the audit of accounts.
@ref s 532(1) The provisions the section applies to (src:7467-7469)
GIVEN `the provision exempts an auditor of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company occurring in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against any liability attaching to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is auditor occurring in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 532(1) the section applies to the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision exempts an auditor of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company occurring in the course of the audit of accounts` OR `the provision is one by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for an auditor of the company, or of an associated company, against any liability attaching to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is auditor occurring in the course of the audit of accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section applies to any provision— (a) ... (b) ..." names these provisions and does not say it applies to no other

-- COVERS-FORK F12: s 532(2), s 532(2)(a), s 532(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: such a provision is void, except as permitted by s 533 (an indemnity for the costs of successfully defending proceedings) or ss 534 to 536 (liability limitation agreements). JUST TRUE means the provision is void.
-- src:7470 | (2) Any such provision is void, except as permitted by—
-- src:7471 | (a) section 533 (indemnity for costs of successfully defending proceedings), or
-- src:7472 | (b) sections 534 to 536 (liability limitation agreements).
@ref s 532(2) Voidness, except as permitted (src:7470-7472)
GIVEN `s 532(1) the section applies to the provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 533 section 532 does not prevent the indemnity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 532(2) the provision is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 532(1) the section applies to the provision`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection makes void "any such provision", that is a provision within subsection (1); for another provision it says nothing
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of provisions within subsection (1)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 533 section 532 does not prevent the indemnity` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such provision is void, except as permitted by— (a) section 533 ..., or (b) sections 534 to 536 (liability limitation agreements)" (an "except" met: fork F6; an answer of NOTHING from s 533 or s 534(2) is read as "not permitted by it", because each permits only what it names: fork F12)
        ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 532(3) where the provision is contained` IS ONE OF
    `s 532(3) in the company's articles`
    `s 532(3) in a contract with the company`
    `s 532(3) otherwise`

-- COVERS: s 532(3)
-- Plain gloss: the section applies to such a provision wherever it is found: in the articles, in a contract with the company, or otherwise.
-- src:7473 | (3) This section applies to any provision, whether contained in a company's articles or in any contract with the company or otherwise.
@ref s 532(3) Wherever the provision is contained (src:7473-7473)
GIVEN place IS A `s 532(3) where the provision is contained`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 532(3) the section applies to the provision wherever it is contained` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 532(3) in the company's articles` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 532(3) in a contract with the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 532(3) otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 532(4)
-- Plain gloss: companies are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate.
-- src:7474 | (4) For the purposes of this section companies are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate.
@ref s 532(4) Associated companies (src:7474-7474)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the one company is a subsidiary of the other` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 532(4) the companies are associated` MEANS
    `coa12 either answer holds` `s 1159(1) the one company is a subsidiary of the other` `s 1159(1) both companies are subsidiaries of the same body corporate`
    -- JUST FALSE here is -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this section companies are associated if one is a subsidiary of the other or both are subsidiaries of the same body corporate" (marginal reading (a): "if" read as closed)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 533  Indemnity for costs of successfully defending proceedings
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 533#L7477, s 533(a), s 533(b)
-- Plain gloss: section 532 does not stop a company indemnifying an auditor against a liability he incurs in defending proceedings (civil or criminal) in which judgment is given for him or he is acquitted, or in an application under s 1157 in which the court grants him relief.
-- src:7477 | Section 532 (general voidness of provisions protecting auditors from liability) does not prevent a company from indemnifying an auditor against any liability incurred by him—
-- src:7478 | (a) in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted, or
-- src:7479 | (b) in connection with an application under section 1157 (power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct) in which relief is granted to him by the court.
@ref s 533 Indemnity for costs of successfully defending proceedings (src:7477-7479)
GIVEN `the liability is incurred by him in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is incurred by him in connection with an application under section 1157 (power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct) in which relief is granted to him by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 533 section 532 does not prevent the indemnity` MEANS
    IF `the liability is incurred by him in defending proceedings (whether civil or criminal) in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted` OR `the liability is incurred by him in connection with an application under section 1157 (power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct) in which relief is granted to him by the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 532 ... does not prevent a company from indemnifying an auditor against any liability incurred by him— (a) in defending proceedings ... in which judgment is given in his favour or he is acquitted, or (b) in connection with an application under section 1157 ... in which relief is granted to him"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 534  Liability limitation agreements
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 534(1)
-- Plain gloss: a "liability limitation agreement" is an agreement that purports to limit the amount of a liability an auditor owes the company for negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in the course of the audit of accounts.
-- src:7482 | (1) A “liability limitation agreement” is an agreement that purports to limit the amount of a liability owed to a company by its auditor in respect of any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust, occurring in the course of the audit of accounts, of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company.
@ref s 534(1) "liability limitation agreement" (src:7482-7482)
GIVEN `the agreement purports to limit the amount of a liability owed to a company by its auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust occurs in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 534(1) the agreement is a liability limitation agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement purports to limit the amount of a liability owed to a company by its auditor` AND `the liability is in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company` AND `the negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust occurs in the course of the audit of accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “liability limitation agreement” is an agreement that purports to limit the amount of a liability owed to a company by its auditor in respect of any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust, occurring in the course of the audit of accounts, of which the auditor may be guilty in relation to the company" (a definition by "is", read as closed: fork F3)

-- COVERS: s 534(2), s 534(2)(a), s 534(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: section 532 does not affect the validity of a liability limitation agreement that complies with s 535 (and any regulations) and is authorised by the members (s 536).
-- src:7483 | (2) Section 532 (general voidness of provisions protecting auditors from liability) does not affect the validity of a liability limitation agreement that—
-- src:7484 | (a) complies with section 535 (terms of liability limitation agreement) and of any regulations under that section, and
-- src:7485 | (b) is authorised by the members of the company (see section 536).
@ref s 534(2) The agreement that stays valid (src:7483-7485)
GIVEN `s 535(1) the agreement complies with section 535 and any regulations under that section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 536(1) the agreement is authorised by the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `coa12 both answers hold` `s 535(1) the agreement complies with section 535 and any regulations under that section` `s 536(1) the agreement is authorised by the members of the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 532 ... does not affect the validity of a liability limitation agreement that— (a) complies with section 535 ... and (b) is authorised by the members"; for an agreement that does not, the subsection says nothing (section 532(2) makes it void unless another route permits it)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the agreement complies with the regulations or is authorised rests on facts not given here

-- COVERS: s 534(3), s 534(3)(a)
-- Plain gloss: such an agreement is effective to the extent provided by s 537.
-- src:7486 | (3) Such an agreement—
-- src:7487 | (a) is effective to the extent provided by section 537, and
@ref s 534(3)(a) Effective to the extent s 537 provides (src:7486-7487)
GIVEN `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 534(3)(a) the agreement is effective to the extent provided by section 537` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such an agreement" means an agreement within subsection (2)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the agreement is within subsection (2) is not known

-- The sections of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 that s 534(3)(b) names, by place.
DECLARE `s 534(3)(b) section of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` IS ONE OF
    `s 534(3)(b)(i) section 2(2)`
    `s 534(3)(b)(i) section 3(2)(a)`
    `s 534(3)(b)(ii) section 16(1)(b)`
    `s 534(3)(b)(ii) section 17(1)(a)`
    `s 534(3)(b) another section`

-- COVERS: s 534(3)(b), s 534(3)(b)(i), s 534(3)(b)(ii)
-- Plain gloss: such an agreement is not subject to ss 2(2) or 3(2)(a) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, nor to ss 16(1)(b) or 17(1)(a) in Scotland.
-- src:7488 | (b) is not subject—
-- src:7489 | (i) in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, to section 2(2) or 3(2)(a) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (c. 50);
-- src:7490 | (ii) in Scotland, to section 16(1)(b) or 17(1)(a) of that Act.
@ref s 534(3)(b) Not subject to the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (src:7488-7490)
GIVEN `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Place of registration`
      section IS A `s 534(3)(b) section of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 534(3)(b) the agreement is subject to the section of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` MEANS
    IF `s 534(2) section 532 does not affect the validity of the agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER place
         WHEN Scotland THEN
             CONSIDER section
             WHEN `s 534(3)(b)(ii) section 16(1)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such an agreement— ... (b) is not subject— ... (ii) in Scotland, to section 16(1)(b) or 17(1)(a) of that Act."
             WHEN `s 534(3)(b)(ii) section 17(1)(a)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in Scotland, to section 16(1)(b) or 17(1)(a) of that Act."
             OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names only ss 16(1)(b) and 17(1)(a) for Scotland
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER section
             WHEN `s 534(3)(b)(i) section 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, to section 2(2) or 3(2)(a) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977"
             WHEN `s 534(3)(b)(i) section 3(2)(a)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, to section 2(2) or 3(2)(a) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977"
             OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names only ss 2(2) and 3(2)(a) for England and Wales or Northern Ireland
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such an agreement" means an agreement within subsection (2)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 535  Terms of liability limitation agreement
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 535(1), s 535(1)(a), s 535(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: an agreement must not cover acts or omissions in the audit of more than one financial year, and must name the financial year it applies to. Whether it also meets the regulations (s 535(2)) is an input.
-- src:7492 | (1) A liability limitation agreement—
-- src:7493 | (a) must not apply in respect of acts or omissions occurring in the course of the audit of accounts for more than one financial year, and
-- src:7494 | (b) must specify the financial year in relation to which it applies.
@ref s 535(1) The terms the agreement must have (src:7492-7494)
GIVEN `the number of financial years for which the agreement applies in respect of acts or omissions occurring in the course of the audit of accounts` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement specifies the financial year in relation to which it applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement complies with any regulations under section 535(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535(1) the agreement complies with section 535 and any regulations under that section` MEANS
    IF `the number of financial years for which the agreement applies in respect of acts or omissions occurring in the course of the audit of accounts` GREATER THAN 1 OR (NOT `the agreement specifies the financial year in relation to which it applies`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A liability limitation agreement— (a) must not apply in respect of acts or omissions occurring in the course of the audit of accounts for more than one financial year, and (b) must specify the financial year in relation to which it applies" (fork F2)
    ELSE `the agreement complies with any regulations under section 535(2)` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the regulations' no, supplied as an input) or NOTHING where the regulations' content is not known (points outside the text)

-- COVERS: s 535(4)
-- Plain gloss: subject to the rest of the section, it does not matter how the agreement is framed.
-- src:7500 | (4) Subject to the preceding provisions of this section, it is immaterial how a liability limitation agreement is framed.
@ref s 535(4) It is immaterial how the agreement is framed (src:7500-7500)
GIVEN `the only difference concerns how the agreement is framed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535(4) the way the agreement is framed affects whether it complies` MEANS
    IF `the only difference concerns how the agreement is framed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the preceding provisions of this section, it is immaterial how a liability limitation agreement is framed."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of how the agreement is framed

-- COVERS: s 535(4)#L7501
-- Plain gloss: in particular, the limit on the auditor's liability need not be a sum of money or a formula specified in the agreement.
-- src:7501 | In particular, the limit on the amount of the auditor's liability need not be a sum of money, or a formula, specified in the agreement.
@ref s 535(4) closing words: the limit need not be a sum or a formula (src:7501-7501)
GIVEN `the limit on the amount of the auditor's liability is neither a sum of money nor a formula specified in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 535(4) the agreement must specify the limit as a sum of money or a formula` MEANS
    IF `the limit on the amount of the auditor's liability is neither a sum of money nor a formula specified in the agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In particular, the limit on the amount of the auditor's liability need not be a sum of money, or a formula, specified in the agreement."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says only that the limit need not be a sum or a formula

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 536  Authorisation of agreement by members of the company
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS-FORK F13: s 536(2), s 536(2)(a), s 536(2)(b), s 536(2)(c)
-- Plain gloss: a private company's agreement with its auditor is authorised by the company's resolution before the agreement waiving the need for approval, or before it approving its principal terms, or after it approving the agreement.
-- src:7505 | (2) A liability limitation agreement between a private company and its auditor may be authorised—
-- src:7506 | (a) by the company passing a resolution, before it enters into the agreement, waiving the need for approval,
-- src:7507 | (b) by the company passing a resolution, before it enters into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms, or
-- src:7508 | (c) by the company passing a resolution, after it enters into the agreement, approving the agreement.
@ref s 536(2) A private company (src:7505-7508)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passed a resolution, before it entered into the agreement, waiving the need for approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passed a resolution, before it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passed a resolution, after it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(2) the agreement between a private company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` MEANS
    IF (NOT `s 4(1) the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A liability limitation agreement between a private company and its auditor may be authorised"; subsection (3) is for a public company
    ELSE IF `the company passed a resolution, before it entered into the agreement, waiving the need for approval` OR `the company passed a resolution, before it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms` OR `the company passed a resolution, after it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A liability limitation agreement is authorised by the members of the company if it has been authorised under this section" (the ways listed are read with subsection (1) as the only ways: fork F13)

-- COVERS-FORK F13: s 536(3), s 536(3)(a), s 536(3)(b)
-- Plain gloss: a public company's agreement with its auditor is authorised by a resolution in general meeting before the agreement approving its principal terms, or after it approving the agreement.
-- src:7509 | (3) A liability limitation agreement between a public company and its auditor may be authorised—
-- src:7510 | (a) by the company passing a resolution in general meeting, before it enters into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms, or
-- src:7511 | (b) by the company passing a resolution in general meeting, after it enters into the agreement, approving the agreement.
@ref s 536(3) A public company (src:7509-7511)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passed a resolution in general meeting, before it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company passed a resolution in general meeting, after it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(3) the agreement between a public company and its auditor has been authorised under this section` MEANS
    IF (NOT `s 4(2) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A liability limitation agreement between a public company and its auditor may be authorised"; subsection (2) is for a private company
    ELSE IF `the company passed a resolution in general meeting, before it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement's principal terms` OR `the company passed a resolution in general meeting, after it entered into the agreement, approving the agreement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A liability limitation agreement is authorised by the members of the company if it has been authorised under this section" (the ways listed are read with subsection (1) as the only ways: fork F13)

-- COVERS: s 536(1)
-- Plain gloss: an agreement is authorised by the members if it has been authorised under s 536 and the authorisation has not been withdrawn.
-- src:7504 | (1) A liability limitation agreement is authorised by the members of the company if it has been authorised under this section and that authorisation has not been withdrawn.
@ref s 536(1) Authorised by the members (src:7504-7504)
GIVEN `s 536(2) or (3) the agreement has been authorised under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(1) the agreement is authorised by the members of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 536(2) or (3) the agreement has been authorised under this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the authorisation has been withdrawn`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it has been authorised under this section and that authorisation has not been withdrawn"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A liability limitation agreement is authorised by the members of the company if it has been authorised under this section" (marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) or (3) is for the other kind of company, or the facts are not given

-- COVERS: s 536(4), s 536(4)(a), s 536(4)(b), s 536(4)(c), s 536(4) defines "principal terms"
-- Plain gloss: the "principal terms" of an agreement are terms specifying, or relevant to determining, the kinds of acts or omissions covered, the financial year it relates to, or the limit on the auditor's liability.
-- src:7512 | (4) The “principal terms” of an agreement are terms specifying, or relevant to the determination of—
-- src:7513 | (a) the kind (or kinds) of acts or omissions covered,
-- src:7514 | (b) the financial year to which the agreement relates, or
-- src:7515 | (c) the limit to which the auditor's liability is subject.
@ref s 536(4) "principal terms" (src:7512-7515)
GIVEN `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the kind (or kinds) of acts or omissions covered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the financial year to which the agreement relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the limit to which the auditor's liability is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(4) the term is one of the principal terms of the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the kind (or kinds) of acts or omissions covered` OR `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the financial year to which the agreement relates` OR `the term specifies, or is relevant to the determination of, the limit to which the auditor's liability is subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “principal terms” of an agreement are terms specifying, or relevant to the determination of— (a) ..., (b) ... or (c) ..." (a list under "are", read as closed: fork F3)

-- COVERS: s 536(5), s 536(5)(a), s 536(5)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the company may withdraw its authorisation by an ordinary resolution at any time before it enters into the agreement or, if it already has, before the start of the financial year the agreement relates to.
-- src:7516 | (5) Authorisation under this section may be withdrawn by the company passing an ordinary resolution to that effect—
-- src:7517 | (a) at any time before the company enters into the agreement, or
-- src:7518 | (b) if the company has already entered into the agreement, before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates.
@ref s 536(5) Withdrawing the authorisation (src:7516-7518)
GIVEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has already entered into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is passed before the company enters into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is passed before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 536(5) the authorisation may be withdrawn by the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has already entered into the agreement`)
    THEN (IF `the resolution is passed before the company enters into the agreement`
          THEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (not an ordinary resolution) or NOTHING where section 282 is not known
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) at any time before the company enters into the agreement" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a))
    ELSE (IF `the resolution is passed before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates`
          THEN `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` -- as above
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the company has already entered into the agreement, before the beginning of the financial year to which the agreement relates" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a))

-- COVERS: s 536(5)#L7519
-- Plain gloss: paragraph (b) has effect whatever the agreement says.
