-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 537  Effect of liability limitation agreement
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 537(1), s 537(1)(a), s 537(1)(b), s 537(1)(c)
-- Plain gloss: an agreement cannot limit the auditor's liability to less than what is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances, having regard in particular to his responsibilities under this Part, the nature and purpose of his contractual obligations, and the professional standards expected of him. What is fair and reasonable is an input (the court's judgment).
-- src:7521 | (1) A liability limitation agreement is not effective to limit the auditor's liability to less than such amount as is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case having regard (in particular) to—
-- src:7522 | (a) the auditor's responsibilities under this Part,
-- src:7523 | (b) the nature and purpose of the auditor's contractual obligations to the company, and
-- src:7524 | (c) the professional standards expected of him.
@ref s 537(1) Not effective to limit to less than a fair and reasonable amount (src:7521-7524)
GIVEN `the amount to which the agreement limits the auditor's liability` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 537(1) the agreement is effective to limit the auditor's liability to the amount agreed` MEANS
    IF `the amount to which the agreement limits the auditor's liability` AT LEAST `the amount that is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A liability limitation agreement is not effective to limit the auditor's liability to less than such amount as is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case" (the judgment of what is fair and reasonable is an input, never guessed)

@ref s 537(1)(a)-(c) Matters to which regard is had (src:7522-7524)
GIVEN `the matter is the auditor's responsibilities under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the nature and purpose of the auditor's contractual obligations to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the professional standards expected of him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 537(1) regard is had to the matter in determining what is fair and reasonable` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the auditor's responsibilities under this Part` OR `the matter is the nature and purpose of the auditor's contractual obligations to the company` OR `the matter is the professional standards expected of him`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "having regard (in particular) to— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." does not close the list

-- COVERS: s 537(2)
-- Plain gloss: an agreement that purports to limit to less than the fair and reasonable amount has effect as if it limited the liability to that amount.
-- src:7525 | (2) A liability limitation agreement that purports to limit the auditor's liability to less than the amount mentioned in subsection (1) shall have effect as if it limited his liability to that amount.
@ref s 537(2) Effect as if it limited the liability to the fair and reasonable amount (src:7525-7525)
GIVEN `the amount to which the agreement purports to limit the auditor's liability` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 537(2) the amount to which the auditor's liability is limited` MEANS
    IF `the amount to which the agreement purports to limit the auditor's liability` LESS THAN `the amount that is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case`
    THEN `the amount that is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case`
    ELSE `the amount to which the agreement purports to limit the auditor's liability`

-- COVERS: s 537(3), s 537(3)(a), s 537(3)(b)
-- Plain gloss: in deciding what is fair and reasonable, no account is taken of matters arising after the loss or damage was incurred, or (whenever they arise) of matters affecting the chance of recovering compensation from other people liable for the same loss.
-- src:7526 | (3) In determining what is fair and reasonable in all the circumstances of the case no account is to be taken of—
-- src:7527 | (a) matters arising after the loss or damage in question has been incurred, or
-- src:7528 | (b) matters (whenever arising) affecting the possibility of recovering compensation from other persons liable in respect of the same loss or damage.
@ref s 537(3) Matters left out of account (src:7526-7528)
GIVEN `the matter arose after the loss or damage in question was incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter (whenever arising) affects the possibility of recovering compensation from other persons liable in respect of the same loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 537(3) the matter is taken into account in determining what is fair and reasonable` MEANS
    IF `the matter arose after the loss or damage in question was incurred` OR `the matter (whenever arising) affects the possibility of recovering compensation from other persons liable in respect of the same loss or damage`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no account is to be taken of— (a) matters arising after the loss or damage in question has been incurred, or (b) matters (whenever arising) affecting the possibility of recovering compensation from other persons liable in respect of the same loss or damage"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only what is left out of account

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 538  Disclosure of agreement by company
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 538(1)
-- Plain gloss: a company that has entered into a liability limitation agreement must make the disclosure the Secretary of State requires by regulations (a note to the annual accounts, or the directors' report, as the regulations say).
-- src:7530 | (1) A company which has entered into a liability limitation agreement must make such disclosure in connection with the agreement as the Secretary of State may require by regulations.
@ref s 538(1) The company must make the disclosure the regulations require (src:7530-7530)
GIVEN `the company has entered into a liability limitation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations made by the Secretary of State require the disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 538(1) the company must make the disclosure the regulations require` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has entered into a liability limitation agreement`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company which has entered into a liability limitation agreement must make such disclosure"
    ELSE CONSIDER `regulations made by the Secretary of State require the disclosure`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the content of the duty is "such disclosure ... as the Secretary of State may require by regulations"; the regulations are outside the sources
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations are outside the sources and their content is not known

